  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 220 PM MDT THU MAY 21 2026\nSunday and Monday see temperatures 10-15 degrees above normal \nas high pressure sits over the area. Afternoon minimum RHs are \ndry at 10-30%, increasing with elevation. The warm weather cools\ndown Monday evening as a cold front moves through, part of a \nlarger upper level low that sits over the area for a few days. \nThe cold front brings wind gusts up to 45 mph Monday and Tuesday\nevenings. While Tuesday will be much cooler, the gusty winds, \ndry conditions, and warm temperatures support elevated fire \nweather risks Monday afternoon and evening. Making the forecast \neven trickier, each afternoon sees a 20-30% chance of \nthunderstorms through the long term as the low pressure keeps \nconditions unsettled. Best storm chances move from the NV border\nSunday/Monday to Central ID Tuesday and most of SW ID Wednesday\nand Thursday. Temperatures gradually warm after Tuesday.",
